  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Given that f: x ↦ (x² − 14)/(5x), x ≠ 0: (i) Calculate f(-4). (ii) Obtain an expression for fg(x) if g: x ↦ x − 1."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: Substituting a negative number needs care with the square; substituting an expression follows exactly the same rule."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p143_q06.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p143-q06 from workbook page 143."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Substitute x = -4 into the numerator.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "(-4)² − 14 = 16 − 14"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: Numerator = 2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Substitute x = -4 into the denominator.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "5(-4)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: Denominator = -20"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Divide to get f(-4).",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "2 ÷ (-20)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: f(-4) = -1/10 = -0.1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 4,
      "instruction": "Form fg(x) by replacing every x in f with (x − 1).",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "fg(x) = ((x − 1)² − 14)/(5(x − 1))"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: ((x − 1)² − 14)/(5(x − 1))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 5,
      "instruction": "Expand and simplify the numerator.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "(x − 1)² − 14 = x² − 2x + 1 − 14"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: x² − 2x − 13"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 6,
      "instruction": "Write the final expression with its restriction.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The denominator 5(x − 1) must not be zero"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: fg(x) = (x² − 2x − 13)/(5(x − 1)), x ≠ 1"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Replace x by -4 in the numerator and denominator separately, then replace x by (x − 1) throughout and expand."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "(i) f(-4) = -1/10 = -0.1  (ii) fg(x) = (x² − 2x − 13)/(5(x − 1)), x ≠ 1."
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "A function rule tells you what to do to whatever sits in the input slot, whether that is a number or a whole expression. Composing means putting the inner function into that slot and tidying up, so the algebra is identical to substituting a number — just longer. The restriction moves with the substitution: f excluded x = 0, so fg must exclude the x making x − 1 zero."
    }
  ],
